+# Recording-engine review-fix report
+
+Scope: recording library/tests only, no App/root/solution changes, no merge. No new dependencies. This report supersedes implementation claims in the original Task2 report but retains its safety incident.
+
+## APIs and semantics
+Public APIs remain FfmpegRecorder(path, root), StartAsync(request, token), BuildArguments, RecordingSession.Completion/StopAsync/CancelAsync/DisposeAsync and existing immutable request/result records. Added internal injectable encoder launcher/process and filesystem boundaries, visible only to the test assembly. Every negative/lifecycle/fault test uses fakes; none can instantiate the production launcher accidentally. The sole real encoding harness independently compares the COMPLETE argument sequence to literal lavfi testsrc/sine-only arguments before production launch. Probe/decode tools receive only that generated output. Tools come from explicit OPENCLICKY_TEST_FFMPEG and OPENCLICKY_TEST_FFPROBE environment registrations. No hardcoded personal install in source.
+
+The locked terminal/publication commit linearizes cancellation: cancellation requested before entering the commit wins; cancellation after terminal commit leaves published output unchanged. Stop is shared/idempotent; dispose is concurrent shared/idempotent. Token cancellation is rechecked immediately before launch; cancellation racing just after that check can briefly launch the declared process, then is observed and cleaned up. This is not an OS-level atomic launch/cancel primitive.
+
+One exit task per process. Bounded stdin, kill, reap and stderr-drain waits; process disposal in finally. Errors and cleanup failures become capped diagnostics. Kill failure can leave a process alive; the result explicitly records kill/reap failures and must not be interpreted as verified cleanup. Delete failure records manual recovery requirement and may leave partial media. No published path on failure/cancel. Final path is separately constructed under canonical root; regression root contains literal .partial.mp4. Executable must be a trusted composition registration, never page/agent supplied. Fixed-local/reparse validation is not a defense against concurrent malicious filesystem replacement.
+
+Recovery is explicitly unsupported in RecordingSession API documentation. Crash orphan partials must never auto-publish, auto-resume, or reopen hardware. Explicit offline caller inspection/deletion only. Limits bound returned final artifacts, not strict OS disk/time quotas; transient overshoot is possible. Audio is explicit DirectShow endpoints; system audio requires an installed/exposed DirectShow loopback endpoint. No WASAPI capability claimed.
+
+## Actual evidence
+All evidence is under tests/OpenClicky.Recording.Tests/evidence/review.
+- red.log/red.exit: expected compiler RED, missing injected constructor, exit 1. Old unsafe tests were replaced BEFORE this first run.
+- green-initial: one fake lifecycle test passed, exit 0.
+- faults.log/faults.exit: actual behavioral RED, 14 passed/1 failed, exit 1. Blocked stdin initially allowed successful publication after forced kill. Fixed by requesting cancellation before kill.
+- green.log/green.exit and final.log/final.exit: all 18 tests passed, exit 0. Final detailed log includes source-bound synthetic receipts, paths, byte sizes, ffprobe full stream/format JSON and durations. Both natural completion and requested stop outputs independently probe video+audio+positive duration and decode to null with ffmpeg exit 0. Fixture media deleted afterward.
+- Matrix: blocked stdin, kill failure, inherited-open stderr, rename/delete failures, cancel-vs-stop, cancel-after-publication, concurrent disposal, nonzero exit, oversize, pre-cancel, consent/source/rectangle/limits validation, executable paths and argument grammar. Kill-failure fixture explicitly asserts process NOT exited rather than claiming impossible cleanup.
+- source-receipt.log contains SHA256 of exact tested production/test sources and final process inventory. No ffmpeg/ffprobe processes observed at receipt time.
+
+## Historical safety incident, preserved honestly
+Original Task2 RED attempted hardware launch under a validation regression. No claim of zero historical capture or zero historical bytes. Parent-discovered 36-byte partial at 09:00:46 was inspected only as an owned test file: hexadecimal content is a 36-byte ftyp header; ffprobe exits 1 with missing moov atom, no readable streams. This artifact alone does not prove what was historically captured, transiently buffered, or deleted. Preserved unchanged. See historical-partial.log.
+
+## Explicit gaps / acceptance boundaries
+No hardware/device enumeration or capture, native UI, app integration, full solution build, parent acceptance, release, or cloud calls. No real crash/kill-failure OS process integration fixture; those faults are fake-injected. Host wall-clock watchdog's full maximum-duration path has not been exercised in a real tool test. Reparse checks are source-reviewed but no dedicated junction fixture added. Deterministic tests cover cancellation before terminal and after completed publication, not every instruction-level scheduler interleaving inside filesystem rename. Full synthetic tests require the two explicit tool environment variables and intentionally fail without them rather than silently skip. Original historical safety gap is not erased by passing safe tests.
+
+Worker stopped/quiescent after scoped commit; no further queued writes or background commands. Parent owns review and integration.
